      "spelleffects": "The Maiden of the Mist's basic attacks apply spell effects as area damage.",
      "onhit": "The Maiden of the Mist's attacks are mitigated by dodge and blind, but not mitigated by block. They also deal 50% damage against turrets.",
      "protection": "The Maiden of the Mist takes 30% damage from lane minions.",
      "abilities": ";Natural Recovery\nThe Maiden of the Mist regenerates 2.5 health per second.\n\n;Endless March\nThe Maiden of the Mist is permanently ghosted and follows Yorick (preferably idle within 100 units of the location 500 units behind him), leashing back to him if he moves 1200 units away from her.\n\n;Touch of the Maiden\nThe Maiden of the Mist's attacks against an enemy champion apply a mark, which is lost from the current target whenever Yorick commands her to a new target or her acquisition of that current target otherwise ends. Yorick's next basic attack or E hit against the marked target consumes the mark to deal bonus magic damage equal to 2 / 2.5 / 3% of the target's maximum health, capped at 30 against monsters.\n\n;Undead Army\nWhenever a nearby enemy dies while there are fewer than 4 Mist Walkers under the Maiden of the Mist's command, she raises another Mist Walker from that enemy's corpse.\n\n;Frenzied\nWhile nearby an enemy marked as Cursed by Mourning Mist, the Maiden of the Mist benefits from the ability's bonus movement speed, and actively seeks to assist Yorick if he is nearby and in combat with an enemy champion. While the Maiden of the Mist is targeting a Cursed unit, an exclamation mark indicator will be visible over her head.\n\n;Hasted\nWhile the Maiden of the Mist is within 2000 units of Yorick, she gains 60 bonus movement speed and benefits from Yorick's flat movement speed bonuses.",
      "notes": "* Unlike other pets, the Maiden of the Mist is not prioritized by turrets over any type of minion.\n* The Maiden of the Mist will level up with Yorick when he does.\n* The Maiden of the Mist will blink to Yorick's location after he completes a Teleport channel."
